WEBVTT

01:31.591 --> 01:33.259
Please…

01:45.814 --> 01:48.566
You screwed up your own suicide, huh?

01:50.068 --> 01:51.319
Kill me…

01:52.695 --> 01:53.780
Please…

02:30.859 --> 02:33.611
I bet you thought
I'd be glad to end your life.

02:38.408 --> 02:39.659
You were wrong!

02:41.744 --> 02:43.830
I hope you suffer in agony

02:46.249 --> 02:47.083
until you die.

03:02.891 --> 03:05.393
I will be despised until the very end

03:09.397 --> 03:12.317
and proudly descend into hell.

04:33.523 --> 04:35.733
Difficulty level, Queen of Clubs.

04:36.359 --> 04:38.319
TARGET

04:38.403 --> 04:40.071
Game: "Target."

04:40.863 --> 04:43.866
Please wait until the game commences.

05:07.390 --> 05:08.641
You thought I'd died.

05:09.642 --> 05:10.727
No way.

05:10.810 --> 05:14.605
You're tough, Ann,
so I was sure we'd meet again.

05:15.898 --> 05:16.899
Tough, huh?

05:19.485 --> 05:23.948
To be honest, I started to believe
it would be easier to wait for death.

05:25.325 --> 05:26.534
Same here.

05:29.329 --> 05:30.663
But we're here now.

05:31.664 --> 05:32.665
Yeah.

05:33.374 --> 05:34.834
Clubs are team competitions.

05:35.710 --> 05:37.628
With the two of us together,
it'll be a breeze.

05:38.421 --> 05:41.257
We're almost there. Let's win this.

05:41.841 --> 05:44.177
Right. You'd better believe we will.

05:50.141 --> 05:52.143
Registration has closed.

05:52.727 --> 05:54.228
The game will now commence.

07:09.095 --> 07:11.097
How long does this go on?

10:40.097 --> 10:41.015
Yo!

10:44.143 --> 10:45.895
So, you've come here too.

10:48.022 --> 10:48.856
Chishiya.

10:49.523 --> 10:51.025
There are just two games left.

10:51.692 --> 10:53.986
All the players are gathering in Shibuya.

10:55.613 --> 10:59.033
I was pretty sure
that you'd be one of the survivors.

11:08.668 --> 11:11.962
You know, you've changed a lot.

11:13.172 --> 11:14.006
You think?

11:14.590 --> 11:15.424
Yeah.

11:16.634 --> 11:17.802
You're mellower.

11:20.888 --> 11:22.473
Mellower?

11:23.474 --> 11:26.268
Yeah, well, I've been through a lot.

11:30.689 --> 11:31.857
Say, Arisu…

11:33.984 --> 11:38.322
Would you mind if I told you something
about myself I've never told anyone else?

11:43.244 --> 11:44.078
Sure.

11:48.749 --> 11:49.667
I…

11:51.627 --> 11:52.711
Yo!

11:56.507 --> 11:59.760
It makes me pretty damn happy
to run into you here.

12:00.928 --> 12:02.096
Niragi…

12:03.055 --> 12:05.266
You intentionally didn't kill me
with that shot.

12:05.349 --> 12:07.560
I wasn't going to end this
with a surprise attack.

12:09.645 --> 12:10.980
Okay, let's begin

12:11.897 --> 12:13.315
a game of shootout.

12:14.316 --> 12:16.652
Now that the three of us
are back together,

12:16.735 --> 12:18.237
that seems most suitable.

12:19.071 --> 12:21.157
A game between players?

12:22.324 --> 12:23.993
The three of us are very similar.

12:24.952 --> 12:27.204
We're oddballs
who can't fit in with society.

12:27.288 --> 12:28.289
We're scum.

12:28.914 --> 12:32.084
Even so, our need to feel alive
is greater than most people's.

12:41.135 --> 12:43.095
I haven't got much time left.

12:44.638 --> 12:46.223
So let's do this.

12:47.099 --> 12:48.225
As kindred spirits,

12:49.101 --> 12:51.020
join me in one final game!

13:07.745 --> 13:08.829
I like it.

13:10.456 --> 13:11.749
Join us, Arisu.

13:12.249 --> 13:13.250
Chishiya?

13:13.876 --> 13:16.378
I'm sure you despise me as well.

13:17.755 --> 13:19.507
Use this opportunity to take revenge.

13:20.508 --> 13:22.426
Let's play a game among the three of us.

13:23.093 --> 13:24.345
Are you insane?

13:25.137 --> 13:27.890
Come on. You've got a gun too. Take aim!

13:29.892 --> 13:31.644
Do we really have to do this?

13:43.614 --> 13:45.866
Niragi, stop this!

13:45.950 --> 13:49.078
I'm simply doing
what I want the way I want!

13:49.745 --> 13:51.372
You guys are the same way!

13:51.455 --> 13:53.040
It's always "Me!" with you two!

13:53.123 --> 13:55.000
It's always about what you want!

13:55.960 --> 13:59.713
You aren't experts on life just because
you saw a bunch of people die!

14:00.464 --> 14:02.383
"Living for others"? That's such bullshit!

14:02.925 --> 14:05.594
All we really care about is
our own selves!

14:05.678 --> 14:07.972
As long as it's good for us,
that's all we need!

14:09.974 --> 14:12.935
And you said
it'll work out if we cooperate?

14:13.477 --> 14:16.522
You just wanted to be
the only survivor in the first place!

14:16.605 --> 14:19.358
I don't want it to end this way!

14:19.441 --> 14:20.943
Do you want to kill us all?

14:21.527 --> 14:22.653
Do it!

14:27.908 --> 14:28.826
Yeah.

14:30.411 --> 14:31.745
You may be right.

14:34.707 --> 14:38.043
Killing each other here
just might be appropriate for us!

14:38.627 --> 14:40.087
At last, you get the picture.

14:44.258 --> 14:45.175
Niragi!

14:47.720 --> 14:50.139
What you said makes the most sense!

14:52.391 --> 14:53.893
You could almost convince me!

15:00.774 --> 15:01.692
But…

15:03.986 --> 15:05.154
I don't ever…

15:06.906 --> 15:09.325
want to go back to being
the weak, selfish person I was!

15:21.128 --> 15:22.171
I won't do this.

15:33.307 --> 15:35.976
I won't pull this trigger
just to help myself.

15:55.663 --> 15:57.122
At last…

15:58.290 --> 15:59.917
I think I've been able to

16:02.127 --> 16:03.754
decide how I want to live.

16:06.048 --> 16:07.299
It's thanks to you.

16:16.350 --> 16:19.937
That sure put a damper on things.

16:24.692 --> 16:25.776
Arisu.

16:34.493 --> 16:35.828
What are you doing?

16:41.667 --> 16:44.628
Oh, yeah, there was you too.

16:47.131 --> 16:48.048
Usagi!

16:48.632 --> 16:49.633
Stop it!

16:49.717 --> 16:51.176
Usagi has no part in this!

16:51.802 --> 16:54.805
Every game needs a heroine
to make it exciting!

16:55.389 --> 16:56.557
This is insane!

16:58.308 --> 16:59.643
If you're dead,

17:00.978 --> 17:03.063
then the three of us
can be kindred spirits again.

17:06.358 --> 17:09.194
I can't stand to be alone anymore.

17:33.719 --> 17:34.845
Chishiya!

17:35.971 --> 17:37.264
Chishiya!

17:37.931 --> 17:40.017
Chishiya! Why did you do that?

17:40.768 --> 17:41.852
Why did you protect me?

17:43.771 --> 17:46.148
I wanted to do something uncharacteristic.

17:48.692 --> 17:51.195
It's probably because of
the people I met here

17:52.529 --> 17:53.781
like Kuzuryu

17:55.282 --> 17:56.492
and Arisu.

17:59.995 --> 18:03.540
Hey, what were you
going to tell me earlier?

18:05.876 --> 18:06.877
Oh, yeah…

18:14.676 --> 18:15.552
To me,

18:18.639 --> 18:21.141
people who live life
so seriously seem like fools.

18:24.311 --> 18:26.647
Those people who strive so hard…

18:27.773 --> 18:29.274
I just want to curse them.

18:31.318 --> 18:33.695
All their goodwill was repugnant to me.

18:37.699 --> 18:39.618
But I must have been jealous.

18:41.620 --> 18:43.789
They had what I didn't.

18:46.500 --> 18:49.628
It seemed like they were criticizing me

18:50.546 --> 18:53.382
for being such a vain and vulgar person.

18:57.302 --> 18:58.470
I was afraid of them.

19:03.392 --> 19:04.476
I know what you mean.

19:08.272 --> 19:10.607
I figured you would say that, Arisu.

19:18.740 --> 19:19.992
Shotguns…

19:20.993 --> 19:22.870
sure don't do a good job of killing.

19:31.044 --> 19:32.212
Even by mistake,

19:34.423 --> 19:36.300
don't you dare ever call me evil.

19:40.679 --> 19:42.431
If there were seven billion of me,

19:45.100 --> 19:48.854
then you'd be the ones who are evil.

19:54.193 --> 19:55.861
It's good for you…

19:58.280 --> 20:00.032
that you're on the side of the masses.

20:45.327 --> 20:46.495
He's coming!

20:50.123 --> 20:51.208
Run!

20:57.381 --> 20:59.466
- Let's move them behind a car.
- Right.

21:19.027 --> 21:21.613
The only blimps left are
the King of Spades and Queen of Hearts.

21:22.322 --> 21:25.534
The surviving players have come
to Shibuya where the blimps are.

21:26.118 --> 21:28.453
We can't go farther
unless the King of Spades is defeated.

21:31.498 --> 21:32.332
Look!

21:37.713 --> 21:39.381
Kuina! Ann!

21:40.966 --> 21:41.967
It's Arisu!

21:48.598 --> 21:49.766
It's been a while.

21:49.850 --> 21:51.685
Thank goodness you're all right!

21:51.768 --> 21:52.853
Good to see you again.

21:53.812 --> 21:55.022
Did you see Chishiya?

21:56.773 --> 21:57.691
Yeah.

22:00.736 --> 22:01.945
He'll be fine.

22:02.612 --> 22:03.447
You're right.

22:04.031 --> 22:06.199
The King of Spades
is trying to end things here.

22:06.908 --> 22:08.160
Let's defeat the King together.

22:39.274 --> 22:40.108
Ann!

23:30.075 --> 23:30.909
Yes!

23:31.535 --> 23:36.206
- We did it!
- Yes!

23:37.332 --> 23:38.416
We did it!

24:17.164 --> 24:18.248
Arisu!

24:39.436 --> 24:40.270
Damn!

25:03.251 --> 25:04.836
- I can't hit him! Shit!
- Let's go!

25:16.765 --> 25:17.599
Arisu!

25:24.105 --> 25:25.106
Over here!

25:32.530 --> 25:33.448
Arisu!

25:37.869 --> 25:38.703
Heiya.

25:40.705 --> 25:41.581
You're Usagi?

25:42.457 --> 25:43.333
Yes.

25:45.085 --> 25:46.169
Nice to meet you.

25:51.591 --> 25:54.594
He's just about run out of
his spare magazines.

25:55.762 --> 25:56.721
Aguni!

25:57.430 --> 25:59.849
Aguni, how'd you get here?

26:02.227 --> 26:03.728
I followed you.

26:05.021 --> 26:06.606
You must like me.

26:10.860 --> 26:13.655
He's still just a human.
He's not omnipotent.

26:14.364 --> 26:17.784
His guns are the same.
They can't be fired forever.

26:18.702 --> 26:20.245
When he's out of rounds, he reloads.

26:21.079 --> 26:24.165
The blimp probably sends them down to him.

26:27.043 --> 26:28.211
We've got weapons.

26:37.637 --> 26:40.056
But these are all the rounds we've got.

26:55.739 --> 26:57.574
Oh, yeah. I've got this.

26:58.783 --> 26:59.659
A good luck charm.

27:00.702 --> 27:02.287
It's a bomb Chishiya made.

27:03.371 --> 27:04.205
Chishiya?

27:05.081 --> 27:06.666
What good is that?

27:06.750 --> 27:08.668
Lure him in and use it at close range.

27:11.421 --> 27:15.175
Judging from the smell,
this bomb's got kerosene in it.

27:15.258 --> 27:16.176
An ANFO bomb.

27:16.801 --> 27:18.928
That won't make much of an explosion.

27:20.513 --> 27:21.973
There's a drugstore over there.

27:22.474 --> 27:25.018
If it's closed off
and filled with aerosol fumes,

27:25.101 --> 27:26.811
the explosion can be amplified.

27:27.562 --> 27:28.438
You sure of that?

27:30.190 --> 27:31.066
Maybe.

27:31.649 --> 27:34.778
In other words,
someone has to lure him in there?

27:35.362 --> 27:36.279
Yeah.

27:36.988 --> 27:39.866
I'll wait for him
in the store and set it off.

27:40.367 --> 27:41.826
But then you'll die, Arisu.

27:42.327 --> 27:44.329
No. I'll get away.

27:44.829 --> 27:45.663
How?

27:46.956 --> 27:48.166
On the second floor,

27:48.666 --> 27:51.878
even if I'm blown outside,
I can still survive.

27:53.922 --> 27:55.006
Maybe.

27:57.258 --> 27:59.344
This is nothing but "maybes."

28:01.054 --> 28:03.807
It's worth betting on his "maybes."

28:05.475 --> 28:08.603
This time, I'll be the decoy.

28:10.355 --> 28:11.940
It's reckless to lure him alone.

28:12.857 --> 28:14.651
I'm enough.

28:16.653 --> 28:18.905
Let's all be decoys.

28:19.614 --> 28:21.908
You'd better believe it.
You can count on us.

28:33.086 --> 28:35.422
Okay. Let's go.

29:00.321 --> 29:03.199
We'll lure him into the alley
so the blimp can't send him ammo.

29:04.409 --> 29:06.369
Then we'll lure him into the drugstore.

29:07.954 --> 29:08.830
I'll sprint for it.

29:09.497 --> 29:12.125
Then you guys enter that alley
and lure him in.

29:12.208 --> 29:13.084
Got it.

29:13.668 --> 29:16.963
Arisu, you fill the store
with aerosol fumes.

29:18.173 --> 29:19.090
Right.

30:26.491 --> 30:27.826
Can't you hit anything?

30:46.469 --> 30:47.554
Watch where you're shooting!

30:49.472 --> 30:50.890
Don't worry! I won't hit you!

33:46.524 --> 33:47.358
Ann!

38:07.159 --> 38:08.077
Shit!

38:11.038 --> 38:11.956
Come on!

38:16.252 --> 38:17.169
Come on.

39:14.894 --> 39:15.728
Come on.

39:16.896 --> 39:17.813
Come on.

40:03.109 --> 40:04.610
Arisu! Do it!

40:07.446 --> 40:08.280
Aguni!

40:09.698 --> 40:10.699
You idiot!

40:13.953 --> 40:14.787
Throw it in!

42:05.689 --> 42:06.607
Aguni!

42:07.733 --> 42:08.651
Go.

42:14.698 --> 42:15.699
What about the others?

42:15.783 --> 42:17.117
They'll be fine.

42:19.078 --> 42:20.663
Go to the final game.

42:44.019 --> 42:44.853
Usagi!

42:49.149 --> 42:50.067
Usagi!

42:52.403 --> 42:53.320
Usagi!

42:55.072 --> 42:56.073
Usagi!

45:08.539 --> 45:10.457
I'm sorry.

45:22.136 --> 45:24.138
That was the only way

45:30.185 --> 45:33.021
I knew how to save you.

45:52.583 --> 45:54.001
I'm sorry.

46:07.931 --> 46:09.766
I never once

46:12.436 --> 46:13.520
hated you.

46:46.011 --> 46:47.596
This isn't fair, you know?

47:17.626 --> 47:18.502
Mori!

47:31.932 --> 47:33.433
Why the hell are you here?

47:35.060 --> 47:36.478
You want me to ask for forgiveness?

47:39.231 --> 47:40.148
No.

47:42.067 --> 47:43.652
I'm the one

47:45.237 --> 47:46.655
who wanted your forgiveness.

47:51.910 --> 47:53.245
For forcing my best buddy

47:54.705 --> 47:56.707
to take on such a shitty role.

48:12.264 --> 48:13.473
Take care of yourself.

49:51.947 --> 49:53.281
Aguni…

50:05.085 --> 50:06.169
Dammit…

50:08.296 --> 50:09.631
I can't get up.

50:13.176 --> 50:14.428
We were…

50:18.640 --> 50:20.058
so close…

50:27.274 --> 50:28.525
You're…

50:29.985 --> 50:31.069
alive.

50:36.283 --> 50:37.451
If we…

50:40.704 --> 50:42.289
meet again…

50:48.336 --> 50:49.755
let's be friends.

51:08.982 --> 51:09.858
Ann…

51:12.277 --> 51:13.278
Ann!

51:14.196 --> 51:15.071
Ann…

51:16.573 --> 51:17.532
Ann.

51:27.584 --> 51:28.418
Usagi!

51:33.381 --> 51:34.466
Usagi…

51:49.105 --> 51:51.024
There is one final game.

51:51.608 --> 51:55.529
All players wishing to register
must do so immediately.

53:13.481 --> 53:14.566
If…

53:15.817 --> 53:18.653
there's a rule that says
the players must kill each other…

53:20.447 --> 53:24.034
I won't hesitate to protect you, Usagi.

53:25.619 --> 53:26.786
You're just…

53:27.662 --> 53:28.914
saying that now…

53:32.083 --> 53:33.835
so you sound cool.

55:06.761 --> 55:10.932
Welcome to the final Game Arena!

57:50.633 --> 57:55.638
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
